            <ArticleTitle>Intestinal volvulus and right-sided blunt trauma: consequence or coincidence?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>363-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two boys developed bile-stained vomiting shortly after being involved in significant right-sided blunt trauma and sustaining fractured right femurs. Both had intestinal volvulus and both had a history of bile-stained vomiting in infancy, which had been investigated and interpreted as normal.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
